# Human Gates

This packet does not authorize any of the actions below. Each requires a separate, explicit
human approval — see ADR-0006 (irreversible actions stay human-gated) and
`06_SECURITY_PERMISSIONS_AND_HUMAN_GATES.md` in the harness guidance.

## Gates carried by this milestone

{{MILESTONE_HUMAN_GATES_LIST}}

## Standing gates (always apply)

- approve the selected milestone before implementation begins;
- approve implementation (permission mode `acceptEdits` or a stricter explicit allowlist —
  never `bypassPermissions`);
- approve any permission escalation beyond the `implement` profile;
- approve push or PR creation (`publish` approval, separate from implementation approval);
- approve resolution of review threads;
- approve merge;
- approve deployment;
- approve any destructive operation;
- perform secret rotation (never automated);
- approve a production image digest, where applicable.

## Fail-closed conditions

Any of the following must stop the run and require a human decision before continuing:
target SHA changes unexpectedly; a secret value is exposed; a required approval is missing; a
required test fails; a required job is skipped; a command lacks provenance; packet validation
fails; the output path escapes the allowed run directory.
